## Step 2: Create Access Connector for Databricks

```
Portal → search "Access Connector for Azure Databricks" → + Create
  Resource Group:  iceberg-poc-rg
  Name:            dbx-access-connector
  Region:          East US 2
```

---

## Step 3: Assign IAM Roles

### Roles for Databricks (Access Connector) on Storage Account
```
Portal → Storage accounts → adlsicebergpoc → Access Control (IAM) → + Add role assignment
```

| Role | Scope | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Storage Blob Data Contributor | Storage Account | Read/write parquet files |
| Storage Account Contributor | Storage Account | Manage storage resources |
| Storage Queue Data Contributor | Storage Account | File event tracking |
| EventGrid EventSubscription Contributor | **Subscription level** | Event notifications |

> ⚠️ EventGrid role must be at **Subscription** level, not Resource Group level

### Roles for Snowflake Managed Identity on Storage Account
Assigned after Step 5 (External Volume creation):

| Role | Scope | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Storage Blob Data Contributor | Storage Account | Write Iceberg metadata |
| Storage Blob Delegator | Storage Account | Generate user delegation keys |

