## Step 4: Create Azure Databricks Workspace

```
Portal → Azure Databricks → + Create
  Resource Group:  iceberg-poc-rg
  Workspace name:  iceberg-poc-dbx
  Region:          East US 2
  Pricing tier:    Premium
```

### 4.1 Setup Unity Catalog

#### Create Metastore
```
accounts.azuredatabricks.net → Data → Create Metastore
  Name:     iceberg-poc-metastore
  Region:   East US 2
  ADLS path: abfss://iceberg-warehouse@adlsicebergpoc.dfs.core.windows.net/metastore/
  Access Connector ID:
    /subscriptions/<SUB_ID>/resourceGroups/iceberg-poc-rg/providers/
    Microsoft.Databricks/accessConnectors/dbx-access-connector
```
→ Assign metastore to workspace

#### Create Storage Credential
```
Databricks → Catalog → External Data → Storage Credentials → + Create
  Credential type:   Azure Managed Identity
  Name:              adls-iceberg-credential
  Access Connector:  /subscriptions/<SUB_ID>/resourceGroups/iceberg-poc-rg/providers/
                     Microsoft.Databricks/accessConnectors/dbx-access-connector
```

#### Create External Location
```
Databricks → Catalog → External Data → External Locations → + Create
  Name:               iceberg-warehouse-location
  URL:                abfss://iceberg-warehouse@adlsicebergpoc.dfs.core.windows.net/
  Storage credential: adls-iceberg-credential
```

> ℹ️ File Events validation may fail — this is OK for batch POC. Skip validation in Advanced options.

### 4.2 Create Classic Cluster

```
Databricks → Compute → + Create compute
  Name:            iceberg-writer-cluster
  Mode:            Single Node
  Runtime:         14.3 LTS (Spark 3.5, Scala 2.12)
  Node type:       Standard_DS3_v2
  Auto terminate:  30 minutes
```

#### Install Libraries
After cluster is created → click cluster name → Libraries tab → Install new:

```
Library 1:
  Source:      Maven
  Coordinates: net.snowflake:spark-snowflake_2.12:2.15.0-spark_3.5

Library 2:
  Source:      Maven
  Coordinates: net.snowflake:snowflake-jdbc:3.14.4
```

Wait for both to show **Installed** status.

