## Key Concepts

### Why Snowflake-Managed Iceberg?
```
CATALOG = 'SNOWFLAKE' means:
  ✅ Snowflake owns the metadata (snapshots, manifests)
  ✅ Data files (parquet) stored in your ADLS
  ✅ No separate catalog service needed (no Polaris, no Glue)
  ✅ Snowflake queries are instant — no refresh needed
  ✅ Full Snowflake features: RBAC, time travel, zero-copy clone
```

### Why Access Connector over Service Principal?
```
Access Connector (Managed Identity):
  ✅ No secrets to manage or rotate
  ✅ Azure manages authentication
  ✅ More secure — no password exposure risk

Service Principal:
  ❌ Client secret must be stored and rotated
  ❌ Secret expiry causes outages
  ❌ More operational overhead
```

### Why Classic Cluster over Serverless?
```
Classic Cluster:
  ✅ Supports Maven JAR installation
  ✅ Supports custom Spark configs
  ✅ Required for Snowflake Spark Connector

Serverless:
  ✅ No cluster management
  ✅ Instant start
  ❌ No custom JAR installation
  ❌ Cannot use Snowflake Spark Connector
```

### Role Summary

| Identity | Resource | Roles |
|---|---|---|
| dbx-access-connector | ADLS Storage Account | Storage Blob Data Contributor, Storage Account Contributor, Storage Queue Data Contributor |
| dbx-access-connector | Azure Subscription | EventGrid EventSubscription Contributor |
| Snowflake Managed Identity | ADLS Storage Account | Storage Blob Data Contributor, Storage Blob Delegator |

